  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the LEDs. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "78916feb-662a-5204-9888-5e03ad5cf131"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 41.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8537d45b-187c-5bfb-b7d8-26f982be38cb"))
  (text "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected, so no series diode is needed on the cell (see docs/standard.md section 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8eb3d768-165b-5286-9e2b-e4ab01495c83"))
  (text "D1 = the chicken's front eye, D2 = its back eye, at the maker's two LED centres. The maker's rev3 had two 5 mm self-cycling RGB LEDs straight on the cell, no resistor." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 147.32 96.52 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "12217804-1f95-5b08-8504-657657b92dba"))
  (text "One 1.3k resistor per white LED: about 0.45 mA each on badge power, about 0.2 mA each on a fresh cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 147.32 100.33 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d6365ebd-e00b-5135-b82a-c19252058bc0"))
